</a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="none" anchor="ctr"/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Answer question:</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" baseline="0" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t> Do electrical cables significantly affect structural dynamics of precision spacecraft?</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" baseline="0" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Status Quo: cable harnesses dynamics unknown and not included in models</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" baseline="0" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Results of this: 1) models overly conservative, 2) isolation system requirements too stringent, 3) control systems have errors and are overly designed.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" baseline="0" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Motivation: Develop techniques and methodologies to incorporate cable dynamics into models in order to reduce conservatism and program risk.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:notes>